.Dd $Mdocdate: August 12 2026 $
.Dt XAICTL 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm xaictl
.Nd dump xAI / Grok Build / developer-API status as sysctl-style key/value lines
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl ajlr
.Op Fl b Ar url
.Op Fl c Ar file
.Op Fl m Ar model
.Op Fl M Ar key
.Op Fl Q Ar text
.Op Fl S Ar id
.Op Fl T Ar team
.Op Fl t Ar secs
.Op Fl -auth Ar path
.Op Fl -refresh
.Op Fl -no-refresh
.Op Fl -refresh-only
.Op Fl -current
.Op Ar prefix ...
.Nm
.Cm query
.Fl Q Ar text
.Nm
.Cm session
.Fl -queries Ar text
.Fl -queries Ar text
.Nm
.Cm data
.Ar ls|lsl|cat|size
.Op Ar store
.Op Ar id
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the single CLI for xAI account and API status.
It merges the former
.Nm grok-sanity
developer-API / harness tools with the former
.Nm xai-status
cli-chat-proxy dump.
Every read-only fact is printed as one
.Cm key=value
line
.Pq sysctl-like ,
suitable for
.Xr grep 1
or
.Xr awk 1 .
.Pp
With no arguments, or with
.Fl a ,
.Nm
dumps every default read-only tree the current credentials can satisfy.
Missing credentials become
.Va prefix.available=false
and
.Va prefix.error=...
rather than aborting the rest of the dump.
.Pp
Positional arguments are key prefixes
.Pq not
.Fl s
section names :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
xaictl xai.credits xai.mgmt.balance
xaictl keyinfo
xaictl keyinfo.team_id
.Ed
.Pp
.Cm query
and
.Cm session
are explicit verbs only.
They burn inference tokens and are never part of
.Fl a .
.Pp
Two credential worlds exist and are both used when present:
.Bl -bullet
.It
Grok Build / consumer:
.Pa ~/.grok/auth.json
.Pq written by Ic grok login
plus optional OIDC refresh against
.Lk https://auth.x.ai .
.It
Developer / management API:
.Ev XAI_API_KEY
and
.Ev XAI_MANAGEMENT_API_KEY
.Pq or Pa ~/.config/cxai/grok.conf
for
.Va keyinfo
and
.Va xai.mgmt.* .
.El
.Pp
Timestamps from the proxy/auth path use
.Sy Date::Manip
in the local timezone:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
YYYYMMDD HHMMSS.<ms> ±HH:MM
.Ed
Each such key also emits
.Va key.raw
.Pq RFC 3339
and
.Va key.unix
.Pq epoch seconds .
Bearer and refresh tokens are never printed.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl a , Fl -all
Dump every default read-only tree.
Implied when no prefix is given.
.It Fl s Ar name , Fl -section Ar name
Extra section or prefix.
Prefer positional prefixes;
this flag is kept for
.Nm xai-status
muscle memory.
.It Fl r , Fl -refresh
Force an OIDC refresh before proxy fetches
.Pq rewrites Pa auth.json
on success.
.It Fl -no-refresh
Never call the IdP and never rewrite
.Pa auth.json .
.It Fl -refresh-only
Refresh or adopt a sibling token, print refresh keys, exit.
.It Fl j , Fl -json
Also emit a compact JSON blob per proxy section as
.Va prefix.json .
.It Fl -auth Ar path
Path to
.Pa auth.json
.Pq default: Pa ~/.grok/auth.json
or
.Ev GROK_HOME Ns /auth.json .
.It Fl b Ar url , Fl -base Ar url
cli-chat-proxy base URL
.Pq default: Li https://cli-chat-proxy.grok.com/v1 .
.It Fl t Ar secs , Fl -timeout Ar secs
HTTP timeout in seconds
.Pq default: 20 .
.It Fl c Ar file , Fl -config Ar file
Developer-API config
.Pq default: Pa ~/.config/cxai/grok.conf .
.It Fl -config-section Ar sec
Config section for the inference bearer
.Pq default: Li creds .
.It Fl -mgmt-section Ar sec
Config section for the management key
.Pq default: Li mgmt .
.It Fl m Ar model , Fl -model Ar model
Model for
.Cm query
/
.Cm session .
.It Fl M Ar key , Fl -management Ar key
Management API key
.Pq or Ev XAI_MANAGEMENT_API_KEY .
.It Fl T Ar id , Fl -team-id Ar id
Team UUID for
.Va xai.mgmt.*
trees.
Else resolved via
.Va keyinfo.team_id .
.It Fl Q Ar text , Fl -query Ar text
Prompt for
.Cm query .
.It Fl -queries Ar text
Repeatable prompt for
.Cm session
.Pq at least two .
.It Fl S Ar id , Fl -session-id Ar id
Grok Build session id for
.Va xai.buildlog
and
.Va xai.signals .
.It Fl -log-file Ar path
.Pa unified.jsonl
path for
.Va xai.buildlog .
.It Fl -current
Use the active session from
.Pa ~/.grok/active_sessions.json .
.It Fl -history-max-sessions Ar n
Cap per-session dump under
.Va xai.history
.Pq default 200 .
.It Fl d , Fl -debug
Verbose developer-API debug.
.It Fl l , Fl -list
List section names and exit.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print a short usage summary and exit.
.El
.Sh SECTIONS
Default
.Fl a
trees
.Pq when credentials exist :
.Cm auth ,
.Cm user ,
.Cm subscription ,
.Cm credits ,
.Cm legacy ,
.Cm autotopup ,
.Cm settings ,
.Cm models ,
.Cm keyinfo ,
.Cm balance ,
.Cm usage ,
.Cm limits ,
.Cm note .
.Pp
Opt-in prefixes:
.Cm history ,
.Cm probe
.Pq Li xai.mgmt.probe ,
.Cm buildlog ,
.Cm signals .
.Pp
Explicit verbs only:
.Cm query ,
.Cm session ,
.Cm data .
.Bl -tag -width xai.billing_legacyXX
.It Cm xai.auth
Local credential metadata from
.Pa auth.json
.Pq no secrets :
scope, mode, user id, email, expiry, proxy base.
Also
.Va xai.date.format
and
.Va xai.date.local_tz .
.It Cm xai.user
.Li GET /v1/user
— profile, principal, team/org, block reasons.
.It Cm xai.subscription
.Li GET /v1/user?include=subscription
plus live
.Va subscriptionTier .
.It Cm xai.credits
.Li GET /v1/billing?format=credits
— weekly/monthly allowance %, prepaid dollars, on-demand caps,
per-product split.
.It Cm xai.billing_legacy
.Li GET /v1/billing
— older monthly-limit / used / history shape.
.It Cm xai.autotopup
.Li GET /v1/auto-topup-rule .
.It Cm xai.settings
.Li GET /v1/settings
— remote flags, access gate, display tier.
.It Cm xai.models
.Li GET /v1/models .
.It Cm xai.history
Composite historical intel
.Pq not in default Fl a :
server monthly dollars, current credits snapshot,
.Pa ~/.grok/logs/unified.jsonl
billing polls, and local session catalog.
Still not a server tokens-per-day ledger.
.It Cm keyinfo
Developer API
.Li GET /api-key
as
.Va keyinfo.*
.Pq team_id, acls, blocked flags, redacted key .
.It Cm xai.mgmt.balance
Management prepaid balance and postpaid preview.
.It Cm xai.mgmt.usage
Management usage analytics for the current month.
.It Cm xai.mgmt.limits
Management postpaid spending limits.
.It Cm xai.mgmt.probe
Readonly GET audit of management endpoints
.Pq not in default Fl a .
.It Cm xai.mgmt.data
Management data stores.
Use the
.Cm data
verb:
.Li xaictl data ls Files .
.Cm ls ,
.Cm lsl ,
and
.Cm size
are
.Cm key=value ;
.Cm cat
prints metadata keys then the raw body.
.It Cm xai.buildlog
Per-turn tokens from
.Pa ~/.grok/logs/unified.jsonl
for
.Fl S
or
.Fl -current .
.It Cm xai.signals
Harness
.Pa signals.json
context-fill for
.Fl S
or
.Fl -current .
This is not SuperGrok consumer quota.
.It Cm query / session
Live inference.
Output is
.Va query.N.*
and
.Va session.usage.* .
.It Cm xai.note
The SuperGrok-not-in-this-API reminder and pointers to
.Va xai.buildlog
/
.Va xai.signals .
.El
.Sh OUTPUT
Lines look like:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
keyinfo.team_id=65c1e471-205f-4566-9c5a-07198bcdf4ce
xai.credits.credit_usage_percent=13
xai.credits.prepaid_balance_usd=0.00
xai.mgmt.balance.prepaid_total_usd=-10.00
xai.buildlog.totals.total_tokens=350
.Ed
.Pp
Money from the proxy is integer cents
.Pq often JSON Li {"val":N} .
Both
.Va *_cents
and
.Va *_usd
are emitted.
Prepaid/top-up cents may be negative on the wire;
Grok Build credit USD uses the absolute value unless noted as signed.
.Sh TOKEN REFRESH
When the Grok Build access token is missing
.Va expires_at ,
hard-expired, or within five minutes of expiry,
.Nm
refreshes automatically unless
.Fl -no-refresh
is set.
The algorithm matches Grok Build
.Ic AuthManager::refresh_chain :
exclusive
.Xr flock 2
on
.Pa auth.json.lock ,
sibling adoption, OIDC discovery, refresh-token grant, atomic rewrite
mode 0600.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width GROK_PRODUCTION_CLI_CHAT_PROXY_BASE_URL
.It Ev XAI_API_KEY
Inference API bearer.
.It Ev XAI_MANAGEMENT_API_KEY
Management API key.
.It Ev GROK_HOME
Root directory for Grok Build config
.Pq default: Pa ~/.grok .
.It Ev GROK_AUTH_PATH , Ev XAI_STATUS_AUTH
Override path to
.Pa auth.json .
.It Ev GROK_CLI_CHAT_PROXY_BASE_URL , Ev GROK_PRODUCTION_CLI_CHAT_PROXY_BASE_URL
Override proxy base URL.
.It Ev TZ
Timezone name used when converting timestamps.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width ~/.grok/auth.json.lockXX
.It Pa ~/.grok/auth.json
OIDC session and optional API-key store
.Pq mode 0600 .
.It Pa ~/.grok/auth.json.lock
Advisory lock coordinating multi-process refresh.
.It Pa ~/.grok/logs/unified.jsonl
Grok Build unified log
.Pq buildlog + history .
.It Pa ~/.grok/sessions/
Per-session
.Pa summary.json
and
.Pa signals.json .
.It Pa ~/.config/cxai/grok.conf
Optional developer-API config
.Pq Li bearer= / Li management_key= .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Pp
.Fl -refresh-only
exits
.Dv 0
on successful refresh or sibling adoption, non-zero on failure.
An unknown prefix exits non-zero.
A default dump that skips trees for missing credentials still exits 0.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Show remaining weekly allowance and prepaid dollars:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
xaictl xai.credits | egrep 'usage|remaining|prepaid|period\\.(start|end)='
.Ed
.Pp
Developer key plus management prepaid:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
xaictl keyinfo xai.mgmt.balance
.Ed
.Pp
Force session renewal without waiting for Grok:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
xaictl --refresh-only
.Ed
.Pp
One cheap inference call:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
xaictl query -Q "Say only hello."
.Ed
.Pp
Current Grok Build session tokens:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
xaictl xai.buildlog --current
xaictl xai.signals --current
.Ed
.Pp
Historical scraps on this host:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
xaictl --no-refresh xai.history > /tmp/xai-history.txt
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Lk https://cli-chat-proxy.grok.com/v1 ,
.Pa docs/xai-status-api.md
.Pq formal HTTP/OIDC spec ,
.Pa docs/journal.md
.Pq grok-build perusal log ,
Grok Build sources under
.Pa crates/codegen/xai-grok-shell/src/extensions/billing.rs
and
.Pa crates/codegen/xai-grok-shell/src/auth/oidc/ .
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Todd T. Fries Aq Mt todd@fries.net
and Grok Build tooling notes.
.Sh CAVEATS
.Bl -bullet
.It
Copying the same refresh token to two machines and refreshing concurrently
can yield
.Li invalid_grant .
Prefer one login per machine, or serialize refresh against a shared
.Pa auth.json .
.It
.Dq Tokens left
in the Grok UI is a percent of the period allowance, not a raw
remaining-token counter.
.It
SuperGrok consumer quota mail
.Pq e.g. 90%
is not exposed by the developer or management APIs.
.It
Requires
.Xr perl 1
with
.Sy JSON::PP ,
.Sy LWP::UserAgent ,
.Sy URI::Escape ,
and
.Sy Date::Manip .
.El
